        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Here is a clear, firm, and professional draft you can send to Ms. Adams:\n\n---\n\nSubject: Clarification Regarding Item Removal and Treatment Instructions  \n\nDear Ms. Adams,  \n\nI am writing to formally address the issue regarding the removal of my refrigerator and other belongings prior to the scheduled treatment.  \n\nAt no point was I informed—either in writing or verbally—that I was not permitted to remove items from my unit. There was no instruction indicating that items such as a refrigerator could not be removed. I made the decision to remove certain belongings strictly to create space for the treatment, as I understood preparation was required.  \n\nWhen I attended your office to request elevator access, there was still no clear communication advising me not to remove any items. The concern about removal was only raised after the fact. A refrigerator and its components are not typically classified as an infringement, and there was no prior indication that doing so would be considered non-compliance.  \n\nI have made every effort to cooperate with management and follow the instructions provided to me. I respectfully ask that you stop attributing fault to me for actions that were taken in good faith and without any prior restriction communicated.  \n\nIf there are specific written policies regarding removal of items during treatment preparation, please provide them to me in writing for clarity moving forward.  \n\nI expect professional and fair communication going forward.  \n\nSincerely,  \nAmit Puri"
          ]
        },
